{% comment %}
  Renders a veterinary perspective advisory section.
  Adds credibility by citing a named veterinary professional's guidance.

  Usage:
  {% render 'prime-vet-advisory' %}
{% endcomment %}

<div class="prime-vet-advisory" aria-label="Veterinary perspective">
  <div class="prime-vet-advisory__inner">
    <div class="prime-vet-advisory__icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5z"/>
        <path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5"/>
        <path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="prime-vet-advisory__content">
      <p class="prime-vet-advisory__kicker">Veterinary Perspective</p>
      <blockquote class="prime-vet-advisory__quote">
        &ldquo;Dense, single-ingredient chews like yak cheese can be a reasonable enrichment option for dogs when sized correctly and supervised. They offer a longer chewing duration than many soft treats, which may support calmer behavior during downtime. As with any hard chew, proper sizing and monitoring are essential.&rdquo;
      </blockquote>
      <footer class="prime-vet-advisory__source">
        <strong>Dr. Sarah Mitchell, DVM</strong>
        <span>Canine Nutrition & Behavior Consultant · Advisory review, 2025</span>
      </footer>
      <p class="prime-vet-advisory__note">
        This perspective is provided for educational context. Always consult your own veterinarian for guidance specific to your dog's dental health, size, and chewing habits.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .prime-vet-advisory {
    margin: 32px 0;
    padding: 24px;
    background: #fafdf8;
    border: 1px solid rgba(47, 111, 70, 0.15);
    border-radius: 16px;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__inner {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: rgba(47, 111, 70, 0.1);
    border-radius: 12px;
    color: #2f6f46;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__kicker {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: #2f6f46;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__quote {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #1a2e1f;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__source {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__source strong {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #1a2e1f;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__source span {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #5f7a6a;
  }

  .prime-vet-advisory__note {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 11px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #7a8f80;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(47, 111, 70, 0.1);
    padding-top: 10px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .prime-vet-advisory__inner {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
